ces may require payment and depend on availability.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"fort-ord-national-monument","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Fort Ord National Monument","title":"Saturday Afternoon: Choose a Fort Ord Trail","subtitle":"Use the federal trail map for an off-campus outing","notes":"Select a route that matches your experience, carry water, remain on designated trails, and review the monument’s trail rules before departure.","short_summary":"A nearby public-land outing with mapped recreation trails through the former Fort Ord landscape.","evidence_claim":"The Bureau of Land Management identifies Fort Ord National Monument as 14,658 acres of public land and provides an interactive map, trail map, and trail rules for visitors.","source_url":"https://www.blm.gov/programs/national-conservation-lands/california/fort-ord-national-monument","source_title":"Fort Ord National Monument","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Review the BLM interactive map and current trail rules first; choose a designated route suitable for your transportation and ability.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"marina-state-beach","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Marina State Beach","title":"Saturday Sunset: Watch from Marina State Beach","subtitle":"End the day at a managed Monterey Bay shoreline","notes":"Arrive well before sunset, stay back from the surf, pack a wind layer, and use the picnic or interpretive areas instead of entering rough water.","short_summary":"A coastal pause centered on dunes, shoreline views, and safe observation rather than water activity.","evidence_claim":"California State Parks lists Marina State Beach as a day-use park open from 8 a.m. to sunset, with beach access, picnic areas, interpretive exhibits, parking, and restrooms.","source_url":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=581","source_title":"Marina State Beach","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Open 8 a.m. to sunset. Strong rip currents make water recreation extremely hazardous, and dogs are not allowed.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csumb-disc-golf-courses","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"CSUMB Disc Golf Courses","title":"Sunday Morning: Play a Short Disc-Golf Loop","subtitle":"Start the final day on one of CSUMB’s campus courses","notes":"Photograph the course map or first tee before starting, keep throws clear of other users, and choose a short loop for a casual introduction.","short_summary":"A self-paced campus recreation stop that works for a small group without requiring a formal competition.","evidence_claim":"CSUMB Recreation states that the campus has two disc golf courses and illustrates the activity with students playing disc golf.","source_url":"https://csumb.edu/recreation/","source_title":"Recreation","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Confirm course locations and any temporary closures with Recreation; yield to pedestrians and follow posted course guidance.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"otter-sports-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Otter Sports Center","title":"Sunday Midday: Learn the Otter Sports Center","subtitle":"Use your student ID for an indoor movement break","notes":"Bring your Otter ID, closed-toe shoes, and a full-length shirt; start with a brief workout and wipe down every station after use.","short_summary":"A straightforward introduction to the student fitness facility and its equipment expectations.","evidence_claim":"CSUMB says the Otter Sports Center is open to its students, is free with a valid Otter ID, and includes strength equipment, cardio machines, a TRX room, and a basketball court.","source_url":"https://csumb.edu/athletics/otter-sports-center/","source_title":"Otter Sports Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Valid Otter ID required. The center closes on campus holidays and home basketball or volleyball game days; verify current hours.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"skylight-transmission-of-knowledge-windows-to-justice","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Skylight: Transmission of Knowledge/Windows to Justice","title":"Sunday Close: Read the CAHSS Mural","subtitle":"Finish at the main entrance of CAHSS Building 504","notes":"Walk the mural from end to end, then use the front-door signage to identify details such as the khipu cords, marigolds, lenses, and scales.","short_summary":"A final reflective stop connecting environmental, cultural, technological, and social-justice imagery.","evidence_claim":"CSUMB documents Johanna Poethig’s acrylic mural Skylight: Transmission of Knowledge/Windows to Justice at the main entrance of CAHSS Building 504 and notes interpretive signage at the front doors.","source_url":"https://csumb.edu/cahss/about/announcements-events/cahss-academic-iii-mural/","source_title":"CAHSS 504 (Academic III) Mural","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View the exterior entrance artwork without blocking doors; interior building access may vary by day and academic schedule.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
